BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 400.87 Tm (stripped first: a $1.2M California home can carry $600-700K of land and only a $300K dwelling, and in the Smyrna) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 385.65 Tm (example a $480K buy minus about 10% land left a $432K dwelling, so 20% equals $86,400, or $7,200 a month over 12) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 370.42 Tm (months [vbHlGVZKjvg @ 00:44:11]. Insurers also push back with "running out of money" while the policy says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 355.20 Tm (unlimited. Wording before the claim call matters too: the claim is on the leak, not the mold, and "flood" versus "leak") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 339.97 Tm (decides eligibility, which is why Ruben pushes a public adjuster and cites a $2,000 claim that became $20,000) Tj ET
