BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 628.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 605.77 Tm (The most expensive firsthand failure on the payer's side is the hotel stay that never ends. Kela Trishaan is working a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 590.55 Tm (file where a family has sat in a hotel for roughly three months, which Trishaan calls a no-no because it risks exhausting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 575.32 Tm (the ALE limit, and three to five dogs made comparable housing hard to find [awTD63In04A @ 00:09:25]. The same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 560.10 Tm (file broke a second way: the family took a pre-planned birthday trip out of town, the trip was denied, and because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 544.87 Tm (hotel was still being paid while they were away, they arguably owe that money back [awTD63In04A @ 00:12:29].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 529.65 Tm (Trishaan's lesson is to ask about trips at the very start, because it is better to have that conversation in the beginning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 514.42 Tm (than to argue about it on the back end. Mike Crowley sets the same ceiling from the agency side: carriers move big) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.20 Tm (losses into a rented house or apartment, and there is no milking a five-star hotel [TkI2Qak3r34 @ 00:01:47]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.97 Tm (furnished alternative looks like Gng. Jackson's employer-provided unit: fully stocked, a new washer and dryer, kids') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 468.75 Tm (beds, welcome food, pet gifts and a gate code [hp6VgBcT7YQ @ 00:04:16].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 453.52 Tm (The second trap is the baseline. Bill Coffman's formula is total expenses minus normal expenses, and the warning is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 438.30 Tm (blunt: if you overestimate your normal expenses, you get shortchanged on your recovery [idtxFNBKKIA @ 00:01:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.07 Tm (Kela Trishaan shows how the adjuster builds that baseline: groceries of $150 to $200 plus DoorDash of $50 to $100,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.85 Tm (only the excess over normal reimbursed, and restaurant patterns checked against where the customer normally eats,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 392.62 Tm (with one or two outlier receipts tolerated but a trend stopped [awTD63In04A @ 00:13:53]. Lydia at Driven Saver got) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 377.40 Tm (six months of extra mileage paid for a commute ten miles farther each way, twenty miles round trip, tracked in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.17 Tm (notebook plus a monthly Excel log of the top three destinations [uCQYAZ1ws_w @ 00:01:11]. The same claim drew) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.95 Tm (an uneven line on replacement items: an antenna and a clothesline were covered, but a dryer was refused, even as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 331.72 Tm (another claimant got rental curtains and bath mats approved [uCQYAZ1ws_w @ 00:02:44]. The operator takeaway: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 316.50 Tm (furnished unit that already includes laundry removes the dryer argument entirely, and every item the family must still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 301.27 Tm (buy needs a receipt and a reason tied to the loss.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 286.05 Tm (The third trap is assuming the clock extends itself. Amy and Sandy Watts at United Policyholders walk through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.82 Tm (California's 24-month minimum and the extension up to 36 months that an insurer shall grant for permit, materials or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 255.60 Tm (contractor delays, then warn that the extension is not automatic, so the family has to ask for it in writing [bPQqrGrXfiI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.37 Tm (@ 00:37:37]. Their discipline is a monthly contact log, letters that open with 'this will confirm', bullet points instead of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.15 Tm (venting, and a ten-business-day reply window before escalating. Corporate relocation payers enforce timing rules just) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.92 Tm (as hard. Henrick Mathieu warns that a misaligned closing date or a new build running behind schedule is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.70 Tm (considered beyond your control under the CAF relocation directives [N4x6hSMmcaM @ 00:05:34]. Operational) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.47 Tm (friction bites too: Nurse Lexi's three-month Hello Landing stay hit a lockbox mix-up and package-pickup headaches) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.25 Tm ([v2OZyLu0O58 @ 00:04:07], and Ashley Bartoletti at Plus Relocation's counter is to print the check-in details,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.02 Tm (lockbox and on-site contact included, before the employee arrives [fv6KqAzMsVI @ 00:00:36]. Bartoletti also flags) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.80 Tm (that the employee usually signs, and that the credit card on file covers damages and incidentals.) Tj ET
